---
import Badge from './ui/Badge.astro'
import s from './Why.module.css'

// Section two: one run accounted for, beside a real comparison with the neighbours. Every neighbour cell is from
// that project's own docs (linked under the table), checked 19 Nov 2026: Node's permission model is opt-in and
// throws ERR_ACCESS_DENIED; Deno denies by default and throws Deno.errors.NotCapable; Bun has no permission model
// in its stable releases. Cells say what a runtime does, never guess at what it lacks.
const cols = ['Node.js', 'Deno', 'Bun', 'jsrt']
const rows: { label: string; cells: (string | boolean)[]; note?: string }[] = [
  { label: 'Host access by default', cells: ['Full*', 'None', 'Full', 'None'] },
  { label: 'Grants live in', cells: ['flags', 'flags', '—', 'a manifest per run'] },
  { label: 'A denied call throws', cells: ['ERR_ACCESS_DENIED', 'NotCapable', '—', 'CapabilityError'] },
  { label: 'npm: and node: modules', cells: [true, true, true, false] },
]
const events = [
  { at: 'rt.fetch', text: 'api.other.com refused', bad: true },
  { at: 'exit 7', text: 'reported as capability' },
  { at: 'report', text: 'outcome, exit_code, killed_by' },
]
---

<section class="section" id="why">
  <div class={`container ${s.wrap}`}>
    <header class={s.head}>
      <Badge>Why jsrt</Badge>
      <h2 class="t-h2">Built for code you don't fully trust</h2>
    </header>
    <div class={s.grid}>
      <figure class={s.item}>
        <div class={`float ${s.run}`}>
          <p class={s.runHead}>
            <span class={s.mark} aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="mono">webhook.js</span>
            <span class={s.ok}>Classified</span>
          </p>
          <dl class={s.facts}>
            <div><dt>Exit code</dt><dd class="mono">7 · capability</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Manifest</dt><dd class="mono">net: app.example.com:443</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <ol class={s.timeline}>
            {
              events.map((e) => (
                <li class={e.bad ? s.bad : ''}>
                  <span class="mono">{e.at}</span>
                  <span>{e.text}</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ol>
        </div>
        <figcaption class={s.caption}><strong>A refusal has a name.</strong> The script can catch the CapabilityError; uncaught, the shell sees exit 7 and the supervisor's report says so, never a crash.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class={s.item}>
        <div class={`float ${s.tableCard}`}>
          <div class={s.scroll} tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="jsrt beside Node.js, Deno and Bun">
            <table class={s.table}>
              <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Behaviour</span></th>{cols.map((c) => <th scope="col" class={c === 'jsrt' ? s.us : ''}>{c}</th>)}</tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {
                  rows.map((r) => (
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="row">{r.label}</th>
                      {r.cells.map((c, i) => (
                        <td class={cols[i] === 'jsrt' ? s.us : ''}>
                          {c === true ? (
                            <span class={s.yes} aria-label="yes">✓</span>
                          ) : c === false ? (
                            <span class={s.no} aria-label="no, by design">✕</span>
                          ) : (
                            <span class={/^[A-Z][a-zA-Z_]+$/.test(String(c)) && c !== 'None' && c !== 'Full' ? 'mono' : ''}>{c}</span>
                          )}
                        </td>
                      ))}
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class={s.caption}>
          <strong>Honest about the neighbours.</strong> Deno denies by default too. jsrt adds a manifest per run, a fixed exit contract and a supervised process, and gives up npm to do it. *Node's docs call its permission model a seatbelt, not a security boundary.
          <span class={s.sources}>Sources: <a class="inline-link" href="https://nodejs.org/api/permissions.html">Node permissions</a>, <a class="inline-link" href="https://docs.deno.com/runtime/fundamentals/security/">Deno security</a>, <a class="inline-link" href="https://bun.sh/docs">Bun docs</a>.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
